Custom Scripts Directory

Place any `.js` files in this folder to load them into the Scripts panel on launch,
or use the Studio tab in the app (templates, Mineflayer docs and a local AI generator).

Each script should export an `info` object and an async `script` function:

```js
const info = {
  name: "Greet",
  default: { interval: 3000 },
  options: [
    { type: "checkbox", label: "Repeat", id: "repeat" },
    { type: "input", label: "Message", id: "message" },
  ],
};

async function script(bot, log, clearLog, getOption, scriptRepeater) {
  if (!bot) return log("Greet: Connect a bot first");

  async function tick() {
    const msg = (await getOption("message", info.name)) || "Hello!";
    bot.chat(msg);
  }

  await tick();
  if ((await getOption("repeat", info.name)) === "on") {
    await scriptRepeater(tick, info.default.interval);
  }
}

module.exports = { info, script };
```

The 6th script argument is `libs` = { goals, Movements, Vec3, mcData }.
Option types: "checkbox", "input" and "select" (with `choices: ["a", "b"]`).

Only run scripts from sources you trust, since custom scripts have full access to the active Mineflayer bot instance and Node.js runtime.
